feat(app-home): Owner's Daily One-Liner — the product's front door

Strategy + Product board mandate (top-3 for both directors): not a
dashboard at 6:47am — a sentence. Felipe opens /app from the truck cab
on his way to the first job and sees:

  TODAY'S BRIEFING
  Good Tuesday morning, Bright Lights.
  6 customers on file · 1 quote in flight · 6 stale units
  Your one move: 6 fixtures aging 220d+ on the shelf · $1,070 tied up.
  Sell these first.                                 [Open inventory →]

components/app/OwnersDailyOneLiner.tsx — pure presentational. Receives
a typed DailyBriefingInput and synthesizes:
  1. Headline based on local time-of-day + tenant name
  2. Body line — facts: customer count, in-flight quotes, drafts,
     visits-this-month, stale units (only includes non-zero items)
  3. "Your one move" — priority-ranked next action with a deep link:
     storm-watch ZIPs > stale inventory > draft quotes > zero customers
     > zero recent visits > generic ("draft a quote you've been
     putting off")
The whole card is a Link wrapping the next-move destination — one tap
from briefing to action.

Wired into app/(authed)/page.tsx populated-tenant branch:
- Three new parallel queries (proposals + visits-this-month +
  stale-inventory units) added to the existing Promise.all so the
  one-liner is a free piece of work alongside what was already fetched.
- Computed inputs: draftQuotesCount, inFlightQuotesCount,
  recentVisitsCount, staleInventoryCount, staleInventoryDollarsCents,
  oldestStaleAgeDays.
- Rendered as the top card on /app home, above StormRadarTile and
  TodayDashboard.

This is the Strategy/Product unanimous "front door" landing — the
product no longer opens with a dashboard, it opens with a decision.
v2 ships per-tenant SMS at 7am ET via Twilio behind the canSend()
gate (TCPA layer already shipped). v3 turns the next-move logic into
an LangGraph agent that reads the audit log + ai_run cost + revenue
trends and writes a more nuanced sentence.

